# Copy this file to .env and add your ElevenLabs API key.
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env
# The key is used server-side only and is never exposed to the browser.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Optional: ElevenLabs voice used for spoken prompts (text-to-speech).
# The default works on ElevenLabs' free plan. Library voices usually require a
# paid plan and will return "paid_plan_required"; the app falls back to your
# device voice in that case. Find IDs at https://elevenlabs.io/app/voice-library
#   Free-plan friendly examples: EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL (Bella), ErXwobaYiN019PkySvjV (Antoni)
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL

# Optional: Google Gemini API key (Google AI Studio). Used server-side for:
#   * speech-to-text (transcription of the patient's voice input), and
#   * the adaptive clinical intake (choosing the next question, flagging warning
#     signs already covered by the rules; it never diagnoses or invents questions).
# If unset, transcription falls back to the browser SpeechRecognition API and the
# intake runs fully rule-based. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: Gemini speech-to-text model. `gemini-3.5-transcribe` is the default.
# GEMINI_STT_MODEL=gemini-3.5-transcribe

# Optional: extra comma-separated terms to bias transcription toward (medicine
# brand names, etc.). A built-in list of common Indian medication names is always
# included; this only adds to it.
# GEMINI_STT_VOCABULARY=MyBrandName,AnotherDrug

# Optional: Gemini model. `gemini-2.5-flash` is used by default.
# On a Google AI Pro account, `gemini-3.8-flash` is a good current choice:
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# Optional: Google sign-in (OAuth 2.0). Leave blank to hide/disable it.
# Create an OAuth client at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# and add an authorised redirect URI matching GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI below.
#   Default redirect URI: http://localhost:3001/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=
